cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CoRTeC: Cohort-Conditioned Differentially Private Synthetic Tabular Data from a Frozen Language Model"
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-09-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Calyie/cortec"
abstract: >-
  CoRTeC spends a differential privacy budget on released statistics rather than on training a
  model: public stratification at zero cost, DP histograms whose L1 sensitivity is 1 regardless of
  bin count, and a conditional target table over a disjoint cell partition that costs one query's
  worth of epsilon however many cells it holds. A frozen, un-finetuned language model generates
  records from those statistics alone, so generation is post-processing and adds no privacy cost.
authors:
  - family-names: "Nnona"
    given-names: "Calister"
